0..40 Comment "// A path whose way back moves a member."
41..43 Comment "//"
44..118 Comment "// The way back defines `answer` as the reply plus one. The answer brought"
119..197 Comment "// there and back is then not the answer, and the reply brought back and there"
198..218 Comment "// is not the reply."
219..221 Comment "//"
222..301 Comment "// The checker refuses each round trip that does not convert, at the member the"
302..376 Comment "// body defines. The refusal marks both endpoints: that definition and the"
377..410 Comment "// member that the theory states."
411..413 Comment "//"
